+---
+description: "Records a persistence type transition and its compatibility acknowledgement."
+kind: persistence-change
+---
+
+# 2026-10-06-workflow-session-mirror
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-06-workflow-session-mirror.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Workflow PTC can retain same-Session private source and invocation backups as workflow-ptc/mirror records when sessionMirror is enabled.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-10-06-workflow-session-mirror
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:workflow-ptc/mirror"
+    previous: null
+    after: "34a6111c01e69df3ca3c45bc5fde702ab9538dddf82e97e024a2328cf8e43d1e"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+The event is required on read, so readers without this vocabulary refuse logs containing it. Existing logs and journal formats remain readable. The host-only projection ignores inherited events from other Sessions. No Session envelope format changes.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+The workflow source suite passes 366 focused tests, including missing-file recovery, cached-prefix reuse, active-run refusal, external-source preservation and detached-history projection recovery. The owned Loader recovery snapshot passes.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
