+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "Claude tool hooks use canonical names and dispatch success and failure to separate events."
+---
+
+# Claude tool hook dispatch
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+`dsh-hooks-claude-code` sends canonical Claude tool names in payloads (`Bash`, `Read`, `Agent`) while accepting both Claude and Harness names in matchers. `PostToolUse` runs only after a dispatched tool succeeds. Failures trigger `PostToolUseFailure`; pre-tool denials trigger neither. Previously post-tool hooks also ran for failures and denials. Stop payloads now report the latest assistant message and track forced continuation within each user turn.
+
+Local agent command and HTTP hooks are mounted during child setup. Project definitions require an exact-directory trust record; malformed local guards reject setup. See [supported local hooks and limits](../../../../packages/hooks/hooks-claude-code/README.md#local-agent-definitions).
+
+Command hooks returning `continue: false` now halt an active prompt, tool or stopping boundary; previously the bridge recorded the request and continued. Stop requests override forced-continuation decisions. A post-tool stop preserves the completed tool result. The durable turn records a hook cancellation; subagent consumers receive `hook-stopped` with retained output, which Workflow accepts like a max-turns result. SessionStart and detached subagent lifecycle events retain their existing context/observer behavior.
+
+`UserPromptSubmit` now defaults to 30 seconds rather than 600 seconds. Successful ordinary stdout from SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit now reaches the model. Cancelled or timed-out command hooks no longer apply JSON control fields even if a signal handler exits zero.
+
+Supported HTTP hooks now run from files and trusted local agents; previously files skipped them and local agents rejected them. Non-2xx and malformed responses remain nonblocking.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Update hook scripts that inspect `tool_name` to accept the canonical Claude names.
+2. Move failure-specific handlers in your hook config to `PostToolUseFailure`. Keep denial handling in `PreToolUse`.
+3. Run a successful tool, a failed tool, and a pre-tool denial; confirm only the intended handlers execute. For Stop handlers, check `stop_hook_active` to self-limit forced continuation.
+
+4. Remove `continue: false` from hooks that intended only to attach context. Check `stopReason` when halting intentionally, and handle `hook-stopped` when consuming subagent results. Confirm the child makes no further model requests, the parent can continue, and a later user turn is still accepted.
+
+`PreToolUse.updatedInput` now changes the dispatched arguments. Hooks run before `tool/call` rather than afterward; effective input is used for audit, UI, concurrency and permission checks. Existing assistant messages are preserved, with a sourced `tool-input-rewrite` correction appended after the result. Remove incidental `updatedInput` fields from hooks that expected them to be ignored. Invalid replacements deny the call; allow does not bypass guards.
+
+Set `defaultTimeoutMs: 600000` in the bridge config to retain the former prompt deadline, or set an individual handler’s `timeout` in seconds. Send diagnostic-only text to stderr. Check that startup/prompt stdout appears in the next request and that timed-out handlers cannot block or inject context.
+
+Remove unwanted HTTP handlers or set `allowedHttpHookUrls: []`. Configure a host URL allowlist and `httpHookAllowedEnvVars` for protected header variables. Verify 2xx JSON decisions and tool denial; non-2xx responses must not block execution.
