+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "Local agent mcpServers fields now activate supported connections and affect child tools."
+---
+
+# Local agent MCP connections
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+The spawn provider consumes mcpServers in local and user agent definitions; previously the field was ignored. A string borrows an already mounted parent-visible server or discovers an approved local/project/user disk configuration. Disk fields expand environment placeholders; newly discovered connections belong to the child. A one-key map activates an inline stdio or HTTP client after origin trust checks. Plugin agent declarations remain ignored.
+
+Clients start before child publication and are owned by that child's scope. Startup cancellation drains negotiated processes; individual failures warn and skip. Definition tools selection precedes MCP additions, while disallowedTools and explicit caller filters remain effective. An explicit tools list that leaves no usable tools rejects startup. Shared resource tools now follow ordinary tools selection and caller allow/deny rules; previously child-owned resource registrations could remain visible after being excluded. ListMcpResources and ReadMcpResource selectors, including their Tool-suffixed canonical names, resolve to the corresponding shared tools.
+
+Resource discovery now accepts an omitted server and returns a flat array of resources with a server field on each item. Previously list_mcp_resources required server and returned a protocol object containing resources. Its cursor argument is removed; the client collects all pages. Exact server names take precedence over normalized names. Failed providers contribute no records, and MCP Apps UI resources are excluded from discovery but remain directly readable. Resource templates and reads retain their protocol results.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Review mcpServers in `.claude/agents/*.md`. Remove previously inert named or inline declarations that should not start a process or contact an endpoint.
+2. Review ~/.claude.json, ancestor .mcp.json files and enabledMcpjsonServers / disabledMcpjsonServers settings for named declarations. Mount shared servers in the parent composition when their connection must survive child disposal, or use a supported inline declaration from a user definition or explicitly trusted project. Check the spawn README for unsupported configuration fields.
+3. Add ListMcpResources or ReadMcpResource to tools when a restricted child needs those operations; server-qualified MCP selectors do not grant shared resource helpers.
+4. Run one child that calls an allowed MCP tool and verify its recorded result. Confirm denied names are absent and child disposal leaves borrowed servers available while closing new connections.
+
+5. Update callers of list_mcp_resources to consume the returned array rather than result.resources. Remove cursor arguments. Use the server field on each resource when calling read_mcp_resource; omit server when discovering all admitted providers.
