+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "Claude agent metadata now controls model requests, iteration limits and argument-bearing tool selection."
+---
+
+# Agent metadata and tool selection
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+The spawn provider reads effort and maxTurns from local, user and plugin agent definitions; previously these fields were ignored. Explicit caller effort wins over the definition, and definition effort wins over parent inheritance. The selected provider validates the resulting effort identifier.
+
+maxTurns counts model iterations, not user turns or tool calls. After the limit, admitted tools finish and the child returns max-turns with its last output. Workflow consumes retained text or captured structured output and caches that value; missing structured output remains null. The child session records SUBAGENT_MAX_TURNS. A child that finishes normally on its last permitted iteration still returns completed.
+
+Tool lists now accept spaces outside parentheses and resolve entries such as `Read(src/*)` to the whole tool. The argument is not a path or command permission: `disallowedTools: Bash(echo:*)` denies all Bash calls. Bash clamps now decode escaped delimiters and reject the inert `Bash(*)` entry.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Review effort and maxTurns in your `.claude/agents/*.md` and plugin agent files. Remove a field to inherit provider defaults or leave iterations unbounded.
+2. Use effort values supported by your selected provider. Invalid frontmatter values warn and are omitted; a valid Claude level unsupported by the provider fails explicitly.
+3. Consumers of SubagentResult must handle max-turns as a limited result with preserved output. Check one capped tool-using child and one normally finishing child; verify the model-request count and returned value.
+
+4. Review argument-bearing `tools` and `disallowedTools` entries that were previously ignored. Use `bashCommandClamp` for command restrictions, with a concrete pattern such as `Bash(git:*)`. If all commands are intentional, use `Bash(**)` instead of `Bash(*)`; existing execution guards still apply. Verify denied tool bodies never run.
