+
+# Workflow admission records
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Uncached agent calls now produce workflow/agent-admission and durable tool-workflow/agent-admission records before waiting for concurrency. They preserve invocation order and failures before a child exists. Older readers that do not recognize the new required event reject these logs. New readers still accept earlier logs; the Session writer version is unchanged.
+
+Default labels now use the first 60 UTF-16 units of the prompt before whitespace normalization. Explicit labels are normalized without truncation, including empty strings. JSON label and phase values accept string conversion; null selects the default.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Upgrade Session readers with the Workflow packages before opening newly recorded runs. Keep older binaries from reading these new logs; no log rewrite is required.
+2. If consuming workflow events, project admission records by seq and update the same row on agent-start. Only published children have a childId; do not expose child controls for queued rows or require agent-end for startup failures.
+3. Run concurrent calls followed immediately by phase(). Verify queued rows precede that later phase and update without duplication, including after replay. See the [persistence acknowledgement](../../../persistence-changes/2026-10-06-workflow-admissions.md).
