+
+# Workflow child tool exclusions
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Workflow children previously inherited orchestration tools unless an explicit caller or agent definition removed them. They now exclude Agent/Task, Workflow and SendUserMessage, including Lab's subagent, subagent_fork and ralph entry points. Agent frontmatter, child-local shadow registrations and tools installed later cannot reopen these names. Ordinary subagent calls keep their existing behavior.
+
+Workflow providers must support toolFilter and enforce its exclude list. A provider without that capability fails before starting a child. The new ToolRestriction.exclude field accepts absent names and applies to inherited, own and future registrations; allow/deny retain their previous inherited-tool semantics.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Move further delegation into the Workflow script's agent(), parallel() or pipeline() calls. Use script-level workflow() for supported nesting.
+2. Update custom Workflow providers to enforce ToolRestriction.exclude across schemas and execution, then declare toolFilter support. Do not enable the capability while ignoring the field.
+3. Verify a Workflow child cannot execute the excluded names even when its agent frontmatter lists them. Confirm the parent retains its orchestration tools and permitted child tools still run.
