+
+# Workflow CLI inputs
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Deployments selecting tool-workflow.inputMode: claude-code expose seven CLI fields and always start background jobs. Separate meta, budgetTotal, workflows and run_in_background fields are rejected. Scripts require a literal metadata header; registered names take precedence over inline code. Description and title are accepted but ignored. CLI registry discovery skips unreadable or oversized files, replaces malformed UTF-8 bytes and preserves earlier definitions when an overriding body has invalid syntax. A sole broken definition is discovered but fails when invoked. Harness input mode retains its existing API.
+
+New PTC Workflow run IDs use wf_ followed by twelve UUID characters. The engine can still read earlier UUID journals, but the CLI model input accepts only the wf_ format. A resumed run retains that ID and receives an independent attempt ID.
+
+CLI scriptPath reads require a single-link regular file with a nonzero identity. The filesystem provider verifies the canonical path against the open descriptor before reading; readable symbolic links still work. Registry discovery and the default harness mode retain their ordinary byte-read behavior.
+
+Explicit CLI scriptPath calls now require a visible Read tool and ordinary Read permission for both the entered and resolved path. Configure permitted outside directories or path-specific Read rules; application adapters can supply bypass mode and added directories through tool-workflow/read-policy. Explicit Read ask/deny rules still reject without a prompt. Network namespace and automount paths are refused before resolution. Engine providers that store private scripts can override sourceDirectories(parent); the PTC provider exposes its owning Session partition.
+
+## Migration
+
+CLI metadata is parsed as strict JavaScript data. Static template strings and optional meta.title are supported; invalid optional annotations and phases without string titles are omitted. Unknown literal fields are ignored, but executable expressions and reserved object keys are rejected. Empty string phase titles remain valid. Discovery can skip body validation only for the native header grammar. The Lab file launcher also uses this mode and its 524288-byte disk limit. The deep-research built-in is available by name; a valid user or project definition can override it, while an invalid override leaves it available.
+
+1. In cordis.yml or the deployment patch, set inputMode to claude-code and keep enableRunInBackground enabled. Lab's code-desktop profile selects this mode.
+2. Move separate metadata into export const meta at the start of each script. Remove the four Harness-only input fields. Pass args as JSON values. The completion notification delivers the result; TaskStop cancels a running task when the job controller enables claudeCodeTaskStop.
+3. Treat returned IDs as opaque. Use the direct engine API or harness input mode to resume older UUID journals; new model calls must use the returned wf_ ID with a source selector.
+4. Confirm malformed inputs start no run, named scripts override valid inline scripts, and accepted calls return a job that remains stoppable after the parent turn ends.
