+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: Workflow execution aligns failure containment, background defaults, recovery and parent-turn output accounting.
+---
+
+# Workflow execution and recovery
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Workflow scripts reject `Date.now()`, `Math.random()`, `Date()` and `new Date()` without arguments. Explicit dates remain supported. See [strict script migration](../workflow-intrinsics/guide.md). Custom compositions mounting `workflow-ptc` now require `tokenMeter` and `sessionProjections`. Workflow results retain their never-rejecting contract; execution errors settle with `stopReason: 'error'`.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Replace implicit clocks and random values in workflow scripts with fields supplied in `WorkflowStartRequest.args`, or the `workflow` tool's `args`. Keep these fields identical when resuming a run.
+2. Ensure custom compositions mount `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-token-meter` before `@deepseek-ai/dsh-workflow-ptc`.
+3. Remote subagent providers used with `budgetTotal` must return `SubagentResult.outputTokens`; local providers use the token projection. Leave the budget unset for remote providers without usage reporting.
+4. Run the script and confirm completion. Repeat with `resumeFromRunId` and confirm unchanged calls are cached. The returned `scriptPath` identifies the saved script. See the [PTC package contract](../../../../packages/workflow/workflow-ptc/README.md).
+5. A pipeline item that becomes `null` no longer enters later stages. Resume retains successful siblings after interrupted calls; a recorded failure or changed invocation invalidates its suffix. Display-only label/phase edits retain cached results.
+6. Consumers displaying usage must treat `tokens` as input/cache/output total and use `outputTokens` for output budgets. Handle optional `tool-workflow/agent-progress` records and skip stall detection when `progressSupported` is false or a tool is still active.
+7. Reuse complete saved scripts via `scriptPath`, or register a literal metadata header in `.claude/workflows` and invoke its `name`. Mount `fs` for file-based entry points.
+8. The workflow tool defaults to background execution. Pass `run_in_background: false` or configure `defaultRunInBackground: false` for synchronous consumers. Mount the jobs registry for background execution.
+9. `parallel()` and `pipeline()` reject exhausted admission before nonempty batches; individual item failures become `null`. Check null results before consuming output. A zero budget disables admission checks.
+10. Configure agent definitions and worktree retention using the [spawn provider reference](../../../../packages/subagent/subagent-spawn-in-process/README.md).
+
+New v2 journals track interrupted starts. Existing v1 journals remain readable but cached results recompute because the invocation key now chains prior calls. Shared output accounting resets on parent turn/start; direct starts outside a turn use independent pools.
+
+Structured output now accepts full object-rooted JSON Schema constraints through Ajv. Invalid output retries are capped at five by default; missing output receives one same-turn reminder. Configuring `maxStructuredOutputRetries` on the spawn provider changes the cap.
+
+Bash command clamps now inspect each command in a list or pipeline. Every raw and resolved span must match a rule; one unmatched command denies the entire invocation before execution. Use `Bash(git:*)` for command prefixes and separate rules for each permitted pipeline program. See the [spawn provider](../../../../packages/subagent/subagent-spawn-in-process/README.md) for syntax restrictions.
+
+Select agent definitions by frontmatter `name`; add required `description` to project/user definitions. Plugin agents use `plugin:directory:name` namespaces and ignore `permissionMode`, `hooks`, and `mcpServers`. Declared skills preload as logged child instructions. Explicit tool lists selecting no installed tools reject startup.
