+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: Workflow scripts use strict JavaScript and frozen intrinsics, and combinators validate dense input snapshots.
+---
+
+# Strict workflow scripts and combinator inputs
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Workflow scripts execute in strict mode. Built-in constructors, prototypes, iterator prototypes and namespaces are frozen; assignment to undeclared variables and inherited read-only methods fails. Ordinary own fields, including Error subclass names, remain assignable. Date constructor aliases cannot obtain current time. Dynamic string evaluation and WebAssembly are unavailable. JSON arguments use the script realm's prototypes.
+
+Combinators snapshot every input slot, ignoring custom iterators and array methods. `parallel()` rejects holes and nonfunctions before invoking any task. `pipeline()` accepts promised items and zero stages; null items skip subsequent stages. Empty inputs return before stage validation and admission checks. Nonempty calls reject exhausted agent or output limits before invoking items. Phase and log objects render as type labels without calling conversion hooks.
+
+Compilation rejects imports, `await using` and identifiers prefixed with `__wRg$`. Async iteration resolves iterator values, including completion and early-return values, and captures iterator methods at the start. Invalid iterator methods or results fail with TypeError.
+
+Host hooks return guest Promises. Their failures expose frozen null-prototype records with name, message, stack and toString; host error codes and custom fields are absent. Child data and completed combinator results are copied into guest objects, preserving cycles and repeated references within one copy. Copies omit function-valued object properties, symbols and __proto__, replace unreadable or function-valued array slots with undefined, and reject nested arrays above 4096 entries. Pipeline stages retain the original item identity until the final copy. Dropped helper rejections are consumed; timer callbacks discard synchronous exceptions.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Declare script variables and replace modifications to shared JavaScript intrinsics with local functions. For an intended own-property override of an inherited read-only method, use `Object.defineProperty` on the instance.
+2. Pass timestamps and seeds through `args`. Use explicit Date arguments and ordinary functions instead of current-time aliases, `eval`, or `Function` string compilation.
+3. Pass dense arrays of functions to `parallel()`. Handle null pipeline results and catch batch admission failures outside the combinator. Do not depend on validation of unused stages when the input is empty.
+4. Format an object's desired phase or log text explicitly before calling the helper.
+5. Rename reserved identifiers and remove imports or `await using`. Return valid iterator records; do not depend on unobserved completion promises or replacing iterator methods after iteration starts.
+6. Catch helper failures by name and message; do not depend on host error codes, prototypes or function-valued result properties. Keep state inside callbacks and return JSON data; copied helper results do not mutate the original items.
+7. Run the updated script and confirm its output and phase labels; repeat a saved run to check deterministic replay. See [workflow execution](../../../../packages/workflow/workflow-ptc/README.md) for configuration and process confinement limits.
