+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "Nested workflow values retain child prototypes, child timers share root lifetime, and child groups and resume keys follow agent calls."
+---
+
+# Nested workflow execution
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Workflow authors receive child-realm objects from nested workflow calls. Agent and combinator results belong to the root realm, including when called inside a child. Nested arguments accept cycles and BigInt through the child copier. A second nested call returns a rejected Promise instead of failing because workflow is absent.
+
+Children now log with [name] prefixes and group agents under ▸ name, then ▸ name #2. Empty child runs emit no phase. Child return or failure leaves timers alive until the root ends. All scripts share timer IDs.
+
+The agent journal chain no longer includes child source or arguments. Existing nested entries may recompute once; subsequent reuse depends on the actual agent prompt and execution options. Journal and Session formats are unchanged. An object selector with name is rejected; use a string name or an object with scriptPath.
+
+Budget objects and timer functions now retain the same references across parent and child scripts. Properties attached to these functions are shared within one run. Replacing a script global does not replace the original object supplied to other scripts.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. In saved workflow scripts, replace workflow({name: "review"}) with workflow("review"). Use workflow({scriptPath: "review.js"}) for a file.
+2. Replace cross-script instanceof Array checks with Array.isArray. Consume cyclic or BigInt child data before returning the root JSON result.
+3. Explicitly clear a child timer when it must stop at child completion. Catch the second-level workflow rejection if the parent should continue.
+4. Update phase consumers for the ▸ name titles and absent empty phases. Verify the first admitted child agent appears in its group.
+5. Resume a completed run and verify unchanged agent prompts and options reuse their results, including after changes to unused child arguments. See the [runtime contract](../../../../packages/workflow/workflow-ptc/README.md#use-this-package).
+6. Move script-local state off budget and timer functions into local variables. Verify child mutations are visible only where deliberately shared; separate runs start with fresh hooks.
