+
+# Workflow output files
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Successful Workflow output files now contain a diagnostic JSON object instead of the raw return value. Read result for the complete script value; absence means undefined, while explicit null remains null. The object also carries the summary, call count, logs, phase and agent records, and available usage totals. Files use two-space indentation without a final newline. Failed or cancelled files are empty; completion events carry their errors. These files are private execution artifacts. The separate [phase migration](../workflow-phase-identity/guide.md) covers Session progress fields; invocation-journal formats are unchanged.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Update readers of WorkflowRun.outputFile to read the result property of successful JSON. Check completion status before parsing; do not parse failed or cancelled files as JSON.
+2. Use workflowProgress for diagnostics. Phase indices start at one and can have gaps for unused reserved child groups. Cached agents omit new usage and duration; missing provider metrics remain absent.
+3. Read the full output path when the displayed result is truncated. Error details come from completion events, not failed output files. See the [runtime contract](../../../../packages/workflow/workflow-ptc/README.md#use-this-package).
