+
+# Workflow phase identities
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Workflow phase listeners receive one announcement per title, including metadata declarations and explicit agent phases. They no longer receive an event for every repeated phase() call. The optional third workflow/phase argument contains the execution-assigned index and optional child kind. Durable tool-workflow/phase events preserve these fields; agent-start records preserve phaseIndex. New indices start at one and can have gaps when an empty child reserves a group. Existing Session records remain readable without these optional fields.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Update progress consumers to retain supplied indices and phaseIndex rather than numbering announcements or inferring agent membership from the most recent event. Metadata declarations and per-agent overrides do not change the script's current phase.
+2. Deduplicate phase titles. Preserve an empty title and the first reserved kind. Sort displayed groups by their assigned indices; concurrent source reads can reserve groups in either completion order.
+3. For older providers or records without indices, retain title-based grouping. Reserved gaps and child markers absent from old records cannot be recovered. Verify repeated titles produce one group and a resumed execution starts its own index space. See the [runtime contract](../../../../packages/workflow/workflow-ptc/README.md#use-this-package).
