+description: Workflow results use sanitized JSON rendering and preserve absent values, while console and failure diagnostics change format.
+---
+
+# Workflow results and diagnostics
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Workflow completion no longer rejects every value that needs JSON conversion. The engine copies enumerable data, removes methods and unreadable properties, ignores toJSON, and serializes sparse or undefined array slots as null. Nonfinite numbers become null; undefined and symbol properties disappear. Date and Map values without enumerable fields become empty objects. Root functions, BigInt, symbols, cyclic results and oversized arrays still fail. Nested returns use the VM copier before the parent performs its final conversion.
+
+A script without a return value now completes with undefined instead of null. JSON envelopes omit that value. The foreground tool omits its result field and Return value section; CLI completion notices omit the result tag. Explicit null remains present. The complete-output JSON omits result when it is absent.
+
+Console methods format JSON data and label unsupported values; warn and error add level prefixes. Script failures use independently read name, message and stack fields, retaining at most five bounded frames. Arbitrary thrown objects no longer execute toString for diagnostics.
+
+Structured agent calls reject missing output after the reminder and exhausted validation; provider API failures and explicit skips return null. A completed child missing its result remains completed in progress, although the script call rejects. Supported in-process Workflow providers now complete the entire tool response: later ordinary tools run, and the last valid structured result replaces earlier captures. A reached retry cap still stops later calls when no result exists. Failed schema calls remain ineligible for cached reuse.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. In workflow scripts, explicitly return null when a downstream consumer requires a present null value. Return plain data instead of relying on prototype methods or toJSON.
+2. In consumers of WorkflowResult, the foreground workflow tool, or CLI task notifications, handle an omitted result separately from null. Read absence from the omitted result field in complete-output JSON.
+3. Update console and error-text assertions to the [engine's formatting contract](../../../../packages/workflow/workflow-ptc/README.md).
+4. Run representative scripts returning undefined, null, sparse arrays and objects with methods. Confirm absence remains distinct from null and that unsupported final values still fail. Existing invocation journals require no migration.
+5. Handle provider-failure null separately from missing-output or validation exceptions around direct schema agent calls. Exercise both results and lifecycle state, multiple valid captures, a later ordinary tool and an exhausted retry cap. Providers opting into outputSchemaCompletion must advertise that capability and receive an outputSchema; omitted completion keeps their existing mode.
