+description: Resumed workflows retain their run ID and use a separate attempt ID for events and journals.
+---
+
+# Workflow resume identity
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+PTC workflow resumes retain the original runId instead of creating another run. Each execution has an optional attemptId on the public handle and observer events; the PTC provider always supplies it, and the Workflow tool persists it. Explicit source paths are returned unchanged. Active runs reject resume until their children and script have settled.
+
+Invocation journals now live in separate attempt files with current.json selecting the latest one. Existing journal.jsonl files remain readable. Older runtimes cannot read the new selector.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Key UI cards, log folds and held execution state by attemptId when supplied; use runId only for legacy records or providers that do not reuse IDs. Keep runId as the resume target.
+2. Retain the entire configured journalDirectory when moving a Session. Do not copy only journal.jsonl or downgrade the reader after creating attempt files.
+3. Stop the previous execution and await its result or disposal before resuming. Check that the resumed handle has the same runId and a different attemptId and that earlier cards remain unchanged.
