+
+# Workflow schema references
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Workflow scripts previously copied the current contents of a schema on each agent call. Root calls now retain the first copy of a schema passed as an own data property; later mutations of the same object are ignored, including repairs after validation fails. A different schema object takes a new copy. Root accessor and proxy option bags do not retain schema references.
+
+Each child invocation owns its schema references before forwarding agent calls to the root, including accessor bags. A new root run or child invocation starts fresh. This changes script input behavior; Session and journal formats remain unchanged.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. In saved workflow scripts, create a new schema object whenever a later agent needs different output fields or validation rules.
+2. After a rejected schema, fix a new object instead of mutating and reusing the rejected object.
+3. Run the script and check that repeated references use the first schema, while replacement objects use the new schema. Check child calls separately. See the [runtime documentation](../../../../packages/workflow/workflow-ptc/README.md#use-this-package).
