+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: Claude Code Workflow mode returns task launch values and completion notifications instead of Harness background envelopes.
+---
+
+# Workflow task protocol
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+`dsh-tool-workflow` with `inputMode: claude-code` returns `status: async_launched`, taskId and taskType instead of kind/jobId. Completion notifications carry the final value directly. The callable `RunWorkflow` alias is absent from advertised schemas. Generic Harness mode is unchanged.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Set `toolName: Workflow` for the canonical model name and enable `claudeCodeTaskStop: true` on `dsh-tool-jobs` for `TaskStop({task_id})`.
+2. Read taskId for cancellation and runId for resume. Update launch-text readers to recognize `Task ID:`, `Script file:` and `Transcript dir:`. Preserve old readers for historical session logs.
+3. Treat `<task-notification>` as an automated event, not user confirmation. Its result is already delivered; read output-file when the displayed value is truncated.
+4. Verify that Workflow is advertised, RunWorkflow executes without being advertised, and disabling Workflow also blocks its alias. Stop a live task and verify cleanup before resuming its runId.
