 <a id="use-this-package"></a>
 ## Use this package
 
+The loop owns ordering between calls: pre-execute is serial; buffered steps finalize in model order, while streaming parallel calls may run post-execute concurrently. Each call still preserves its own pipeline order.
+
 Mount `dsh-tools` wherever agents call tools: it provides `ctx.tools`, the registry every tool plugin registers into and the loop dispatches through. Registering a tool is enough to make it visible — the registry feeds its schemas into the system-prompt assembly automatically.
 
+Tool definitions may declare `aliases`. Only the canonical name appears in model schemas and the PTC SDK; every alias resolves to the same visible definition. Allow, deny and exclude restrictions naming either spelling apply to the whole tool. Canonical names win over aliases across scopes; otherwise the nearest visible registration wins. Duplicate names or aliases in one scope are rejected. Execution records retain the caller’s spelling, so name-based policies resolve it through `tools.get(name, agent)?.name`.
+
 ### Register a tool
 
 `defineTool` builds a typed tool definition: a model-facing name, description, and parameter schema, a canonical output declaration, and an `execute` body that returns only the declared JSON value. Model arguments are validated before execution; invalid input becomes a normal error result.
