 Omission of `retryPolicy` uses normal mode: five retries for `EMPTY_RESPONSE`, `RATE_LIMIT`, `SERVER`, `TIMEOUT`, and `TRANSPORT`, with bounded exponential backoff from 500 ms to 10 seconds and 10 percent jitter. Normal mode can change its finite budget, eligible codes, and backoff; always mode asks downstream recovery first, then retries every model-request failure without an attempt limit, stopping only on success, cancellation, or plugin disposal.
 
+Normal mode optionally selects `strategy: claude-code`: ten retries, 500 ms exponential backoff capped at 32 seconds before positive 0–25% jitter, and `Retry-After` as a floor on that local delay. Provider `providerRetryable` takes precedence over the code allowlist when present. Existing budget and backoff fields remain configurable. Delays above the runtime timer limit (2147483647 ms) delegate instead of overflowing the timer; configured exponential caps plus jitter must fit that limit.
