 <a id="use-this-package"></a>
 ## Use this package
 
+Discovered MCP tools with `annotations.readOnlyHint: true` participate in the bounded parallel tool pool. False or absent hints remain exclusive. The annotation is captured for each discovered tool generation and refreshed on a tool-list change; it does not bypass tool approval or guards.
+
 Add `dsh-mcp-client` when the model should call tools from an external MCP server as if they were native. Give each server a unique name and transport. The official SDK selects the 2026-07-28 protocol when available and falls back to supported legacy revisions. Choose stdio for a local program and Streamable HTTP for a service; stdio negotiation starts a temporary probe process before the serving process.
 
 ### Minimal configuration
@@ -92,6 +94,8 @@ The server's tools appear before the harness starts its first turn. When the ser
 
 When a server connection drops — for example a local server process crashes — the plugin reconnects automatically with delays that double from 500 ms up to 30 s and then refreshes the tool set; reconnect progress is visible in the logs. During an outage the last known tools stay listed but calls to them fail until the server recovers. After ten consecutive failed attempts the server's tools are removed and reconnection stops until you reload the configuration or restart the harness; a server that stays connected for a while resets that counter. Set `reconnect.enabled: false` to disable automatic reconnection — tools then stay listed but fail until you reload. Editing the configuration entry reloads the server connection in place, and unchanged names stay unchanged.
 
+Programmatic child composition can call activateMcpClient with a schema-resolved Config and McpClientAdmission. Its startup signal closes and drains negotiation before rejecting; once ready, the caller's effect scope owns the connection. acceptTool filters public names before registration on every discovery, notification and reconnect. resourceTools selects shared resource operations before registration; omitted allows all and an empty list allows none. getMcpServerContext returns a borrowed visible server, including servers with no tools. inheritMcpServer mirrors source-visible tools and context into another scope, keeps the supplied admission rule during updates, intersects requested resource operations with source visibility and server admission, and removes only borrowed registrations on disposal.
+
