+Providers must explicitly advertise `streamToolCalls` before a caller can request `agentOptions.streamToolCalls: true`; support for `agentOptions` alone is insufficient. The service rejects unsupported requests before startup. Spawn and fork implement this one-shot capability. Streaming dispatch is not implicitly inherited from the parent, and this flag does not define a provider retry or transport fallback policy. Continuable starts reject the option until their durable descriptor can restore it.
