+Capabilities declare agentType, worktree isolation, Bash clamps and outputSchemaCompletion independently. A response-completion request requires both a schema and provider support; the last valid result in that response wins. SubagentResult.failure carries a machine code, HTTP status and retry delay; toolCalls optionally reports calls handled before the terminal boundary.
+
+Provider requests may include `agentType` and `isolation: "worktree"` only when the provider advertises the corresponding capability. Built-in providers do not advertise these options. Remote providers can report cumulative output for that child run as `SubagentResult.outputTokens`; workflow budgets require this when no local token projection exists.
+
 This package is the contract every delegation setup shares. You enable it by mounting the service together with one or more provider backends and the model-facing delegation tool; from then on, an agent can delegate work and the service routes each request to the named provider.
 
