 ### Calling the tool
 
-The model submits three parameters plus one flag: `meta` (required identity data: `name`, `description`, and optional `whenToUse` and `phases`), `script` (required plain JavaScript body — no `export const meta` statement; its parameter description carries the body rules and the tool description carries the hook contract), `args` (optional JSON object exposed to the script as the `args` global; wrap a bare list in a field so the wire schema stays honest), and `run_in_background` (optional; present only while `enableRunInBackground` holds).
+CLI metadata accepts static template strings and an optional meta.title for display. It drops mistyped optional annotations and phase entries without string titles, preserves empty phase titles, and rejects expressions or reserved object keys even in ignored fields. Full parsing uses strict JavaScript; header-only discovery falls back to full parsing for syntax outside the native static subset. The harness input mode retains its separate parser.
+
+The CLI catalog includes deep-research without disk configuration. Valid user and project scripts override the built-in; invalid overrides retain it. The built-in scopes a string question, pipelines searches and deduplicated fetches, ranks up to 25 claims, and requests three independent verifier votes per claim. Two refutations reject a claim; insufficient votes remain unverified. Synthesis returns citations, caveats, source counts and vote results. High-relevance sources can exceed the nominal 15-fetch budget. Child providers need usable web search and fetch tools for live research.
+
+In claude-code mode, explicit scriptPath reads require Read in the calling Agent’s scoped tool catalog. The tool applies [Claude Read settings](../../settings/claude-code-config/README.md#lookup) before opening the source, then rechecks the resolved target before reading bytes. UNC, NT namespace and automount paths are refused before filesystem resolution. The tool-workflow/read-policy waterfall supplies application Read availability, bypass mode and added directories; listeners delegate with next(). Without a listener, only ordinary cwd/private reads and settings grants apply. Private directories come from workflowEngine.sourceDirectories(parent), mapped into the active filesystem. Inline and registered-name invocations do not require Read. Direct resolveWorkflowSource callers supply their own authorize callback when they need Agent permission checks.
+
+`inputMode: claude-code` exposes only script, name, description, title, args, scriptPath and resumeFromRunId. Every accepted call starts an owned background job; enableRunInBackground must remain enabled. Description and title are ignored. Scripts require a leading literal metadata export. Nonempty paths take precedence over names, and names over inline scripts; an explicit inline script is validated even when another source supplies the executed body. Empty path/name selectors are absent. Names and paths reject control/invisible characters; inline scripts reject control characters except tabs and line feeds, and are limited to 524288 UTF-16 code units. Resume IDs must match `^wf_[a-z0-9-]{6,}$` and require a source selector. Registry entries use .js files, including readable symlinks. Discovery skips unreadable or oversized entries and reads metadata without parsing bodies; a broken overriding body keeps the earlier definition, while a sole broken definition reports its syntax error at invocation. CLI file decoding replaces invalid UTF-8 bytes, with the byte cap enforced before decoding. Cancellation still aborts discovery. The engine still receives separate body and metadata. The default inputMode, harness, retains the extended inputs below.
+
