+{
+  "initial": [
+    {
+      "name": "TaskStop",
+      "description": "Stop a running background task by its task_id. Returns its task identity and status after cleanup.",
+      "parameters": {
+        "type": "object",
+        "properties": {
+          "task_id": {
+            "type": "string",
+            "description": "ID returned by the tool that launched the background task."
+          },
+          "shell_id": {
+            "type": "string",
+            "description": "Deprecated: use task_id instead."
+          }
+        },
+        "additionalProperties": false
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "name": "Workflow",
+      "description": "Starts a background workflow and returns a task ID immediately. Its completion notification includes the return value. Use TaskStop({task_id}) to cancel.\n\nRun a JavaScript workflow script that orchestrates subagents at scale. Use this for work that fans out across many independent pieces — an audit over many files, a migration, multi-angle research, adversarial verification of findings — where you write the orchestration as a script instead of delegating turn by turn.\n\nScript-body hooks:\n- `agent(prompt, opts?): Promise<any>` — run one subagent to completion. Without `opts.schema` it resolves to the child's final text; with `opts.schema` (an object-rooted JSON Schema supporting references, combinators and value constraints; formats are annotations) it resolves to the validated object. Resolves `null` when the child fails (filter with `.filter(Boolean)`). Other opts: `label` (display), `phase` (progress group), independent `provider`/`model` LLM target overrides, `effort` (low/medium/high/xhigh/max), provider-gated `agentType`/`isolation: \"worktree\"`, `stallMs`, `disallowedTools` and `bashCommandClamp`.\n- `pipeline(items, ...stages): Promise<any[]>` — run each item through the stages independently with NO barrier between stages (prefer this for multi-stage work). Each stage receives `(prev, item, index)`. A stage throw or null result drops that ITEM to `null` and skips its remaining stages.\n- `parallel(thunks): Promise<any[]>` — run zero-argument functions concurrently and await ALL of them (a barrier; use only when a stage genuinely needs every prior result together). A throwing thunk resolves to `null`.\n- `workflow(name, args?)` — run a named or {scriptPath} child workflow one level deep, sharing concurrency, count and budget.\n- `budget.total`, `budget.spent()`, `budget.remaining()` — parent-turn output allowance and live usage; omitted or zero budget disables admission checks. Date.now(), Math.random(), Date() and no-argument new Date() throw; pass timestamps via args.\n- `phase(title)` — start a progress phase; `log(message)` — narrate progress; `args` — the tool call's `args` input, verbatim.\n\nparallel/pipeline await all items and turn any individual failure into `null`; uncaught errors outside those combinators end the script. The script has setTimeout/clearTimeout and console log/info/warn/error/debug; timers are disposed when the script settles. Filesystem, network and Node.js APIs are unavailable; agents do the work.",
+      "parameters": {
+        "type": "object",
+        "properties": {
+          "script": {
+            "type": "string",
+            "maxLength": 524288,
+            "description": "Self-contained JavaScript. Begin with a literal export const meta = { name, description, phases }, then the workflow body."
+          },
+          "name": {
+            "type": "string",
+            "description": "Registered workflow name. Takes precedence over inline script; scriptPath takes precedence over both."
