+
+# 2026-10-06-streaming-tool-history
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-06-streaming-tool-history.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Adds required stream-start and stream-merge events for request-owned tool execution before response completion. The merge names the earlier start, full attempt, and every advertised assistant message. An optional non-streaming transport on the start records a provider-owned complete-response fallback.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-10-06-streaming-tool-history
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:assistant/stream-merge"
+    previous: null
+    after: "f8db08d7fdd43aeccf0b98f6d789016e0d76cad9e5aec6668ac2712b7161120c"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:assistant/stream-start"
+    previous: null
+    after: "5743206777e1525b827a5a2b3a94f69d5344b9ab5169b0a3ddeae67b53f95e0b"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Existing V4 headers, envelopes, surface event types, and message payloads remain unchanged. New logs write a required stream-start before any intermediate message; older vocabularies reject that event even in an incomplete log. Omitted transport means the ordinary stream; the only explicit transport is non-streaming. Current readers validate the merge and reconstruct one assistant response before its tool results. No released codec or historical generation changes. A full assistant/attempt retains the original stream; the new events scope intermediate messages so usage is counted once.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+Focused scheduler, cancellation, restoration, token-meter, and persistence runs passed 259 tests in 15 files and 122 tests in 7 files. Four strict physical-restoration checks include older-vocabulary refusal for complete and unfinished logs. A later 112-test run covers actual local HTTP stream retries, complete JSON fallback, rejection before tool execution on malformed complete output, terminal failure after an accepted conclusion, and Workflow child retry suppression. Consumer and SDK checks are recorded separately. The rebuilt 32-package installation passes 14 actual-process comparisons against the recorded Claude CLI reference and 170 installed smoke checks. All 29 Workflow Loader scenarios and all three corpus gates pass; 672 replay-consumer checks also pass. Broader browser acceptance is recorded separately.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
