+
+# Review trusted Claude command hooks
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+The Claude hook bridge runs registered command hooks with host filesystem access, matching their trusted configuration. Previously these calls inherited the Shell deployment default, which could reject hook writes even in a full-access session. An agent's read-only or workspace-write setting still confines model tool calls; it does not restrict trusted hook commands. Shell credential scrubbing, timeout and cancellation remain active.
+
+User-agent definitions are trusted. Project-agent hooks still require explicit trust for the exact project directory; plugin-agent hooks remain ignored. Codex hooks retain the executor's default policy. See [Claude hooks](../../../../packages/hooks/hooks-claude-code/README.md).
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Review commands in your configured `hooks.json`, settings hooks, and trusted `.claude/agents/*.md` definitions as executable host code. Remove commands whose trust depended on the model tool sandbox.
+2. Custom compositions with a confining Shell must provide `sandboxPolicy`, as the shipped sandbox Shell already requires. The bridge uses this service to resolve the explicit hook execution policy.
+3. Run a hook that writes an intended marker and confirm its `hook/result` exit code is zero. Separately verify that a model tool write still fails in a read-only session.
