+
+# Read sessions with streaming tool execution
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+`AgentOptions.streamToolCalls: true` enables tool execution before response completion. Their Session logs include required `assistant/stream-start` and `assistant/stream-merge` events. Readers without these events reject the log, including unfinished requests. Buffered agents keep their existing event sequence. Session remains V4; released codecs and historical files are unchanged. See the [compatibility record](../../../persistence-changes/2026-10-06-streaming-tool-history.md).
+
+Intermediate assistant messages are response segments. Consumers must use the Session surface or the merge decision to reconstruct one response before its tool results. The full `assistant/attempt` owns token usage and live stream settlement. Token-meter invalidates its older projection checkpoints and replays the log. New starts and merges carry matching `incompleteBlocks: discard` policies; unsuccessful unclosed blocks stay in the full attempt but are excluded from history and output. Omission preserves old partial-text behavior. Readers of a settled suffix use the merge policy. Text-only retries after closed text also append a logged `stream-recovery` user instruction. Update readers together; older streaming readers cannot reconstruct these new failed responses.
+
+Workflow enables this mode for capable subagent providers. DeepSeek stream failures, including a terminal envelope with an unclosed content block, can retry once and then use a complete JSON response; the corresponding start event carries `transport: non-streaming`. Update the LLM service and DeepSeek adapter with the consumers below. Failed complete responses and failures after an accepted tool conclusion are terminal.
+
+DeepSeek preserves tools between thinking blocks and retains received signatures in failed-stream metadata. After content starts, direct adapter consumers must inspect the terminal reason rather than expect a thrown error. Complete-response validation remains atomic.
+
+Update the Messages adapter when restoring opaque responses: `redacted_thinking.data` is retained in adapter-private replay metadata beside an empty reasoning block. Older adapters cannot replay that payload. Requests now omit other-model thinking, empty reasoning without usable metadata, and a trailing thinking-only assistant turn. These projections leave the Session unchanged, so switching back to the original model restores its thinking.
+
+Thinking rejection repairs add required `assistant/reasoning-strip` events in streaming and buffered sessions. Older readers reject these logs. Update Session and adapters together to retain tool order when repairing legacy responses. Update the Session reader with the Messages adapter and AgentLoop: the event preserves raw responses while omitting selected reasoning and its replay entries from later requests. Direct adapter consumers receive `REASONING_REPLAY_REJECTED` with recovery coordinates; persist the decision before retrying, or surface the failure. See the [compatibility record](../../../persistence-changes/2026-10-07-reasoning-recovery.md).
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Update Session readers, AgentLoop, token-meter, Session Controller, Chat, Trajectory, and both SDKs together before enabling `streamToolCalls` in agent creation code.
+2. Update custom transcript and usage consumers to recognize both stream markers. Use `Session.deriveMessages()` for model history; do not count each intermediate assistant message as a separate model attempt.
+3. Verify a completed and an interrupted streaming session through the current Session reader. Existing buffered sessions require no conversion. Keep a reader supporting the new events when opening newly recorded streaming sessions.
