+# Consume streaming tool results by call ID
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Agents using `streamToolCalls: true`, including capable Workflow children, finalize parallel tool pipelines concurrently. Their post hooks may overlap, and durable results and additional contexts follow pipeline completion order. Completed results remain visible while a later call awaits input preparation or approval. Assistant calls and pre-execute retain model order. An exclusive tool waits for every earlier pipeline, including post hooks. Buffered agents retain model-order finalization.
+
+Discovered MCP tools with `annotations.readOnlyHint: true` now participate in the bounded parallel pool. Missing or false hints remain exclusive; the hint does not authorize execution or bypass policy. See [MCP client](../../../../packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md) and [AgentLoop](../../../../packages/core/agent-loop/README.md).
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Correlate tool results using `toolCallId`, not array position. Use the recorded result order when replaying a session.
+2. Make streaming post hooks safe for independent concurrent invocations; do not rely on another tool's post hook running first.
+3. Keep dependent tools exclusive or issue them in separate requests. Cancellation still drains started pipelines, and exclusive barriers include post-hook completion.
+
+The Session event fields and format are unchanged. Existing logs keep their recorded ordering.
